ck.\n\nI also made the box classification sturdier:\n- **Marker box:** a box whose interior objects are all single cells.\n- **Motif box:** a box that contains at least one multi-cell object.\n\n## The rule (unchanged)\n\n1. The input shows a striped wallpaper with two framed rectangles on it.\n2. One rectangle holds complete motifs. Each motif has a unique \"anchor\" colour:\n   - pair 1: the 8 under the `2.2/222` cup;\n   - pair 2: the 1 at the centre of the 8-plus;\n   - test: the 6 in `.1./161/111`, and the 7 in `555/575`.\n3. The other rectangle holds lone marker cells of those anchor colours.\n4. The output is the marker rectangle, cropped with its frame.\n5. For each marker, copy the motif whose unique anchor has the marker's colour, placed so the anchor lands on the marker.\n\n**On the test input:**\n- The marker box is the 2-framed box with interior 8.\n- It holds markers 6, 7 and 6.\n- The 1-ring motif goes on each 6, and the `555/575` cap goes on the 7.\n- The result is a 9×14 grid.\n\n**Stages emitted:**\n1. The cropped marker box.\n2. One stage per stamped motif.\n3. The final grid.","code":"def transform(grid):\n    g = np.array(grid)\n    H, W = g.shape\n    seen = {}\n    for c in np.unique(g):\n        for comp in components(g == c):\n            y0, x0, y1, x1 = bbox(comp)\n            if y1 - y0 < 2 or x1 - x0 < 2:\n                continue\n            Y0, X0, Y1, X1 = y0 - 1, x0 - 1, y1 + 1, x1 + 1\n            if Y0 < 0 or X0 < 0 or Y1 >= H or X1 >= W:\n                continue\n            per = np.concatenate([g[Y0, X0:X1 + 1], g[Y1, X0:X1 + 1],\n                                  g[Y0:Y1 + 1, X0], g[Y0:Y1 + 1, X1]])\n            f = per[0]\n            if not np.all(per == f) or f == c:\n                continue\n            seen[(Y0, X0, Y1, X1)] = int(c)\n    info = []\n    for (Y0, X0, Y1, X1), c in seen.items():\n        inner = g[Y0 + 1:Y1, X0 + 1:X1]\n        objs = objects(inner, bg=c, diagonal=True, multicolour=True)\n        if objs:\n            info.append(((Y0, X0, Y1, X1), c, objs))\n    marker = None\n    motif = None\n    for it in info:\n        if all(o[\"size\"] == 1 for o in it[2]):\n            if marker is None or len(it[2]) > len(marker[2]):\n                marker = it\n        else:\n            if motif is None or sum(o[\"size\"] for o in it[2]) > sum(o[\"size\"] for o in motif[2]):\n                motif = it\n    (Y0, X0, Y1, X1), mc, mobjs = marker\n    (PY0, PX0, PY1, PX1), pc, pobjs = motif\n    out = g[Y0:Y1 + 1, X0:X1 + 1].copy()\n    emit(out, \"Crop the framed box that holds only single-cell markers, frame included.\")\n    temps = []\n    for o in pobjs:\n        temps.append([(y, x, int(g[PY0 + 1 + y, PX0 + 1 + x])) for (y, x) in o[\"cells\"]])\n    for o in mobjs:\n        my, mx = o[\"cells\"][0]\n        col = int(g[Y0 + 1 + my, X0 + 1 + mx])\n        for t in temps:\n            anchors = [(y, x) for y, x, v in t if v == col]\n            if len(anchors) == 1:\n                ay, ax = anchors[0]\n                for y, x, v in t:\n                    ty, tx = 1 + my + y - ay, 1 + mx + x - ax\n                    if 0 <= ty < out.shape[0] and 0 <= tx < out.shape[1]:\n                        out[ty, tx] = v\n                emit(out, f\"Stamp the motif whose unique colour-{col} cell lands on the marker at ({my},{mx}).\")\n                break\n    emit(out, \"Final: every marker replaced by its matching motif.\")\n    return out\n","candidate_tactics":{"selection":[{"source":"verified program checkpoint","text":"Stamp the motif whose unique colour-8 cell lands on the marker at (3,10)."},{"source":"verified program checkpoint","text":"Stamp the motif whose unique colour-8 cell lands on the marker at (3,14)."},{"source":"verified program checkpoint","text":"Stamp the motif whose unique colour-8 cell lands on the marker at (4,3)."}],"template":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"Pair 2's motif box has a frame of colour 1, and each motif inside it (an 8-plus) has a 1 at its centre."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"- **Motif box:** a box that contains at least one multi-cell object."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"Each motif has a unique \"anchor\" colour:"}],"topology":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"I had rejected any box whose interior contains the frame colour, so this box was thrown away."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"That check was not needed: a real interior is already pinned down by its colour component plus a uniform frame one cell outside it."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"- **Marker box:** a box whose interior objects are all single cells."}],"crop":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"The output is the marker rectangle, cropped with its frame."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"The cropped marker box."},{"source":"verified program checkpoint","text":"Crop the framed box that holds only single-cell markers, frame included."}]},"provenance":{"reference_assisted":false,"query_labels_used_for_rule_diagnosis":false},"artifact_sha256":"52693bc13b184b9b6bdfcaa65ea19b8387ff4201d75d67af5573346c94d19fb4","task_sha256":"f0cd406e452c34d50593507f1082e4a92d7514ba5fed7466da449dbda98bd193","validation":"Frozen corpus recorded successful replay on teaching fixtures; synthetic generalization not established."}
